{
  "_id": "bhCrimsonRite000",
  "name": "Crimson Rite",
  "ownership": {
    "default": 0
  },
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You learn to invoke a rite of hemocraft that infuses your weapon strikes with elemental energy. As a Bonus Action, you can activate a rite you know on one weapon you're holding. The rite lasts until you finish a Short or Long Rest. When you activate a rite, you take Necrotic damage equal to one roll of your Hemocraft die (@scale.blood-hunter.hemocraft-die). This damage can't be reduced in any way.</p>\n<p>While the rite is active, attacks you make with that weapon are Magical, and they deal extra damage of the rite's type equal to one roll of your Hemocraft die (@scale.blood-hunter.hemocraft-die). A weapon can hold only one active rite at a time, and no other creature can gain the benefit of your rite.</p>\n<p>You know one Primal Rite of your choice from the list below. You learn another Primal Rite at 7th level, and you gain access to the Esoteric Rites at 14th level.</p>\n<p><strong>Primal Rites</strong></p>\n<p><em><strong>Rite of the Flame.</strong></em> The extra damage is Fire damage.</p>\n<p><em><strong>Rite of the Frozen.</strong></em> The extra damage is Cold damage.</p>\n<p><em><strong>Rite of the Storm.</strong></em> The extra damage is Lightning damage.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
